WEBVTT

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.040
What? A massive Roman Army
contingent has appeared

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.360
at the Seize border with No Man's Land?

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.580
Aisha!

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.520
What was that gunshot?

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.150
We've secured a Roman soldier!

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:43.710
Are they dead?

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.480
No, still breathing.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.830
Well done!

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.460
We will now rendezvous with the
1st and 3rd divisions on the border-

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.890
What are you doing-

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:54.800
Don't move!

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.240
Move and I'll shoot.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.530
Captain!

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.160
Colonel, please escort your
men outside the fortress.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.170
Fill the Blue Sky

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:11.070
What's going on?

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.750
Betrayal!

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.720
The girls took our commander hostage
and barricaded themselves in the fort!

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.190
What?

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.430
Fortunately, it missed her internal organs.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.960
Then, for the moment, she should be OK.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:28.690
Thank you, Yumina-san.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.320
Well done.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.340
She'll be a sacrifice to start the war.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.500
She'd be worth less to us dead.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.280
What is going on here?

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:48.800
For the last month, we've followed the
approaching Roman army from the rear.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.590
It's probably nothing more than a display of power
to give them an advantage in the peace talks.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.740
They must think we're fools.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.220
But the Archduke insisted we do nothing.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:05.480
So we needed something to
push them to attack us.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:11.110
Like a sobbing POW executed
right in front of them.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.520
You can't intend to-

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.020
The peace talks are a farce!

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.030
Rome must be destroyed!

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.380
Isn't that right, Noël Kannagi?

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:24.660
No, my dear ally, the witch of Helvetia.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:27.540
You thought I wouldn't notice?

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:28.710
Stop!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:31.960
You just used her!

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:37.670
Noël-san, you have something to do
with the Invisible Reaper?

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.470
Invisible Reaper?

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:45.150
That girl there was one of the greatest
geniuses in academy history,

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:51.470
the one who revived the Invisible Reaper,
an old-era bioweapons plant.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:55.170
Your talent is still valuable.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.920
Come back to me.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.990
Kureha-chan, toss him in the
underground distillery.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:14.350
My comrades are already deploying
to fight the Romans.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.880
One small spark is all that's needed.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.970
Back to the battlefield, huh?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.660
I thought it was finally over...

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.520
We've both got crap for luck.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:32.520
I've locked the Colonel inside the distillery.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.000
Thank you, Kureha-chan.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.770
Have something to eat...

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.920
Some cookies I got at Treize!

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:49.700
They're good.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:51.960
Naomi-san, you're still here?

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.790
I'll leave if it gets dangerous.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.780
This is really messed up!

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:03.330
The Flame Maidens are supposed
to protect the city.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.830
We're getting them involved in battle!

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.590
Um, about that...

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:15.680
When I was hiding, I asked Aisha-san about
the legend of the Flame Maidens.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:21.740
And she said that the Romans tell
a totally different legend...

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:23.580
What kind?

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:27.740
The Flame Maidens protect others' lives.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.020
Wh-What?

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.030
It's time to switch.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.160
I'm OK!

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.850
I don't trust you out here.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:59.660
For starters, can you even
fire a gun at anyone?

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.690
If I think it's the right thing
to do, I might be able to.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.090
Really?

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:11.190
I'm a fortress maiden, too!

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:14.810
Like our forerunners, the Flame Maidens...

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:15.940
What?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:20.350
You believe that arbitrary
Roman fairy tale?

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:20.880
Yes.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.880
It feels right to me.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:27.000
The Flame Maidens protect others' lives.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.670
I think that just might be the case.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.140
What's wrong?

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.300
I can hear it...

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.140
Hear what?

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:51.370
Kanata!

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.750
I don't care how good her ears are,
she can't hear you from here.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.380
A signal to stop fighting?

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.480
Yes! I heard it!

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:08.920
Really?

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.260
I'm sure!

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.540
It's too early to be happy about it.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:17.530
She might have imagined it,
and even if not,

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:20.740
we don't know it means the
peace talks are over.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:23.730
Anyway, we need to tell Colonel Hopkins-

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.000
Big trouble!

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.190
I went to take food to the
Colonel, and he was gone!

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:33.640
I'm glad you're safe!

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.990
We strike in ten minutes.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.260
Colonel!

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.810
Do you really think they'll listen?

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.290
It's worth a try.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:51.260
Roger.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:52.960
It's useless.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.990
The Colonel was laughing...

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:03.480
When he saw my Reaper
kill all those people,

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.820
he was laughing so hard...

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:13.990
He'll kill... He'll fight until no one is left.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:18.270
But I helped him.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.890
It's my fault.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:26.050
If you think that, then save more
lives than you've taken, Noël-san.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.470
Aisha...

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.120
Cease-fire?

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.220
Impossible!

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.830
But her ears are that good!

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:38.570
That's right!

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.000
We'll vouch for her!

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.000
She's a tiny kid, and she forgets stuff,

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.970
and isn't sexy at all!

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:47.040
She wouldn't lie!

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.620
Arrest everyone here!

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.940
Do you want war that much?

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:55.490
War advances civilization and science.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:08:00.960
I want to bring back the glory
humanity once had.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.210
What?

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:07.130
The Romans are going to attack
tomorrow morning!

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:12.470
Then, there's no way to stop the war.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.720
Naomi-san was arrested.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:30.280
Let's go.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:30.990
It's impossible!

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:33.980
It's the Demon of Vingt!

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:37.630
But I want to deliver the
sound I've been given!

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:38.780
That's just selfish!

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.290
It's selfish!

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.790
How can you make that decision yourself?

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:44.870
We're soldiers!

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:50.490
Someone was saying the world is ending.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:54.840
But I like this world.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.590
I like this town.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.850
I love the people here.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:03.600
I can't give up.

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.610
Kanata...

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.860
Please.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:11.230
Stop the war.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.600
Aisha-san was saying the same thing.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.480
But I...

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.960
As a soldier, I have killed people, too.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.690
I'm just like you.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:44.550
I'm...just like...you.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.830
You have suffered enough.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.400
You have suffered enough.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:58.820
So even if no one else forgives you, I will.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:03.650
So even if...

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:22.990
You forgive me?

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:30.070
Thank you, Aisha.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:35.440
If we do this, there'll be no turning back.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.150
You're OK with that, right?

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.160
Yeah.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:51.920
Then I've got nothing else to say.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.590
Do what you want.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:57.770
Thank you, Kureha-chan.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:03.960
For our sakes, you've always said
what you thought was best, right?

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.140
But I...

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:14.940
I don't want a girl my age
to be tortured, either!

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.790
But Rio-sempai's gone...

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:23.490
And Noël and Kanata are such slackers...

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:28.490
So I thought I had to do my best...

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.400
I'm sorry I'm such a bad captain.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:35.130
Kureha-chan.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.970
Let's go, everyone.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:49.090
May all of the Gods grant their
blessings to the Flame Maidens.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.810
Primary converter reactor output rising.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:04.340
FAP, FAC, DMR, ECP all normal.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:07.620
Superconductor circuit functioning
within stable parameters.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:11.020
Fire control system's looking good.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:14.320
Primary and secondary cannons are online!

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.250
Release all joint locks!

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:26.260
W-Weight reduction system online.
Coefficient is around five.

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:29.260
Ready to go.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:32.830
If we just do it like in training, we'll be fine.

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:35.570
Let's go, my girls!

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:36.610
Right!

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.140
Prepare to fire main cannon!

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:39.780
Load AP round!

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.780
AP round loaded!

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.380
Target locked!

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.700
Kana-chan, the signal!

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:54.460
Right!

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.970
"Begin the attack"?

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:16.940
Fire!

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:54.020
It's Kanata-neechan!

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.730
The Takemikazuchi...

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:00.480
They've restored so much of that
ancient high technology.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.320
Contact all tanks!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.990
Do everything you can to stop them!

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.460
Begin the attack!

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.740
We won't let you through!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.530
We don't want any more war!

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:11.240
Don't stop them!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.830
You'll have to take us out first!

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:15.530
That's right!

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:16.870
Now, what will you do?

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:19.250
Demon of Vingt.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:34.520
Circle around!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.720
We'll meet up with the forces to our rear!

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:45.600
The Flame Maidens protect others' lives.

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:50.530
The rest is in your hands, Kanata-san.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.270
Many years ago,

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:01.290
before the world became as it is now,

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:06.450
God sent an angel to punish the world.

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:11.530
The angel was wounded, and set his wings
down to rest, at a western-end town.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:22.520
It was the maidens, who lived in the
city's fortress, that saved him.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:27.010
He was sent to destroy them,

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:32.250
but they took pity on his wounds

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:39.270
Gaining the help of a giant spider,
they gave the angel refuge at the bottom of the valley.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:47.580
Each, in turn, embraced the angel's neck,
to keep the blood from pouring out.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:55.020
In return, he gave them a golden horn.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:16:04.120
But eventually, the townspeople found
him there. They set fire to the valley.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:13.260
Burning the maidens, and
taking the angel's head.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:23.370
The legend says that then armies
of angels appeared, covering the sky.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:26.500
But then a miracle occurred.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:30.140
A glorious sound filled the air,

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:32.010
and the angels left.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:45.270
The last maiden had used her last breath
to sound the golden horn.

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:01.250
Hey, you remember that girl?

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:03.660
The one you gave the caramel to?

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:07.460
She'll be caught up in this, too, won't she?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:09.780
All troops, prepare to charge!

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:12.100
Nothing to do about it.

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:13.740
We're soldiers.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:18.520
Charge!

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:29.860
What?

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:34.460
What's that?

00:17:37.390 --> 00:17:38.570
It's an allied tank!

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.160
It's with...

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.240
The 1121 Platoon!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.600
It's the cease-fire signal!

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:06.650
No...

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:08.780
It's a Roman military signal!

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:11.870
Commander!

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.010
We can't stop here!

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:14.400
Ready the main cannon!

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:18.410
No... They won't stop.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:19.530
Captain!

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.670
Kana-chan!

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.250
That girl...

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:15.990
What are you doing?

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.330
Attack!

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:18.890
Fire! Fire!

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:20.720
Both sides, lay down your weapons!

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:40.650
I am second heir to the royal line of Helvetia

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:43.800
and fiancée to the Holy Roman Emperor.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:46.300
Rio Kazumiya Arkadia!

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:52.820
I command you by the names of my father,
the Archduke of Helvetia, and of the Roman Emperor!

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:54.810
The peace talks have ended.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:57.460
There is to be no more fighting!

00:20:57.910 --> 00:21:00.300
Both sides are to disband immediately!

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:02.890
This is a royal order!

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:07.350
Those who disobey will be punished by

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:10.580
the first Helvetia Royal Guard,
in both leaders' names!

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:12.240
Impossible...

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:18.980
Then...

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:22.060
We don't have to fight!

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:53.870
Miss!

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:56.370
Miss!

00:21:58.250 --> 00:21:59.660
Sergeant!

00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:30.730
Spring sure has sprung.

00:22:31.430 --> 00:22:32.990
Hey, Noël,

00:22:32.990 --> 00:22:35.520
that letter Aisha sent you...

00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:37.340
What did it say?

00:22:37.340 --> 00:22:43.220
My wounds are healed, and I'm practicing
the trumpet every day.

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:43.220
Translate it!

00:22:43.220 --> 00:22:46.090
She's doing well and practicing her trumpet.

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:48.220
Yeah? Great!

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:55.540
Man, we get letters from Rome
but not from the capitol.

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:57.730
I'm sure she's busy.

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:00.230
She's a princess now.

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:04.730
But even on the battlefield,

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:08.080
she was surrounded by guards,
and we couldn't talk to her.

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:10.490
It's Claus's bike!

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:20.020
She's here! She's here!

00:23:20.020 --> 00:23:22.480
I can't tell you how much I've been
looking forward to the new girl!

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:24.090
I'm going to be really hard-

00:23:43.210 --> 00:23:50.400
I am Lt. Rio Kazumiya Arkadia. I have been transferred
to the 1121 Platoon as of today.

00:23:51.130 --> 00:23:54.410
Captain Filicia Heidemann, please
give me permission to arrive.

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:56.430
Very well.

00:23:56.430 --> 00:23:59.910
We don't use ranks here, Rio.

00:24:00.400 --> 00:24:02.120
Um, well...

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:07.020
The Roman Emperor is actually a decent guy.

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:12.430
He said he'd grant any wish I had,
as a reward for stopping the war.

00:24:13.400 --> 00:24:15.160
And so...

00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:20.050
Welcome back.

00:24:20.050 --> 00:24:21.190
I'm home.

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:22.920
Welcome back!

00:24:24.380 --> 00:24:26.680
Welcome back, Rio.

00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:40.070
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to
people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
